WEBVTT

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.820
Your next favorite skincare ingredient may
have been invented by bacteria

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.430
trying not to die,
not snail mucin,

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.020
not salmon DNA, and not
another form of hyaluronic acid.

00:00:10.826 --> 00:00:15.856
This tiny molecule helps microorganisms survive
places so salty and so

00:00:15.856 --> 00:00:19.696
dry that an ordinary cell would
lose its water and stop functioning.

00:00:20.224 --> 00:00:23.804
And it is now turning
up quietly in Korean serums,

00:00:24.034 --> 00:00:25.424
creams, and sunscreens.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.004
It is called Ectoin.

00:00:28.004 --> 00:00:30.064
And the real science is
stranger than the market.

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:35.399
Ectoin is what researchers
call an extremalite.

00:00:35.479 --> 00:00:37.239
That sounds like a superhero.

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:41.719
It just means a protective molecule
made by microbes living somewhere extreme.

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:45.623
The bacterium we get most of
it from has a name,

00:00:45.623 --> 00:00:47.503
Halomonas elongata.

00:00:47.503 --> 00:00:48.533
It lives in salt.

00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:50.643
When the salt outside gets punishing,

00:00:50.763 --> 00:00:52.453
it floods itself with ectoins.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.310
Why?

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.740
Because salt pulls water
out of cells.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.520
Lose enough water and proteins
start to lose their shape,

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.957
membranes get unstable, and
the cell stops working.

00:01:02.977 --> 00:01:06.957
keeps the space around
those fragile structures survivable.

00:01:06.977 --> 00:01:09.957
Which led skincare researchers
to an obvious question.

00:01:09.977 --> 00:01:12.957
Could it do the same
for stressed human skin?

00:01:13.455 --> 00:01:18.165
Here is where ectoin stops
behaving like a normal moisturizer.

00:01:18.165 --> 00:01:22.805
A familiar humectant like glycerin or
hyaluronic acid attracts water and

00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:24.175
holds on to it.

00:01:24.345 --> 00:01:28.315
Ectoin seems to work on how
water arranges itself around proteins

00:01:28.315 --> 00:01:29.765
and membranes.

00:01:30.517 --> 00:01:33.747
Scientists call the idea preferential exclusion,

00:01:33.747 --> 00:01:35.107
the tidy version.

00:01:35.247 --> 00:01:38.347
Acton protects proteins by
staying off their surface,

00:01:38.347 --> 00:01:40.747
which helps the water
around them stay organized.

00:01:41.214 --> 00:01:44.414
The honest version is messier.

00:01:44.414 --> 00:01:48.424
In the simulations, ectoin also showed
some attraction to that surface.

00:01:48.694 --> 00:01:51.494
And how far it stays back
depends on how tightly the

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.934
protein's own water is already arranged.

00:01:54.518 --> 00:01:57.898
Think of a celebrity inside
a ring of security.

00:01:57.948 --> 00:01:59.978
Ectoin is not hugging the celebrity,

00:02:00.038 --> 00:02:02.718
it hangs back and helps
the ring hold its shape,

00:02:02.978 --> 00:02:07.559
which is why calling it another
hydrating ingredient misses the interesting part.

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:10.679
Your outer skin barrier
is under constant load.

00:02:11.419 --> 00:02:14.509
Dry air, cleansing, pollution, sun,

00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:16.379
strong actives.

00:02:16.579 --> 00:02:21.119
When it struggles, water escapes more
easily and skin can feel

00:02:21.119 --> 00:02:24.379
tight, rough or unusually reactive.

00:02:24.597 --> 00:02:28.987
This lab research suggests Ectoin can
help stabilize biological structures and

00:02:28.987 --> 00:02:31.667
improve hydration in that outer layer.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:34.017
One study found it
changed how keratin,

00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:36.377
the main protein in
our outer skin cells,

00:02:36.507 --> 00:02:37.607
behaves with water.

00:02:38.203 --> 00:02:41.283
Though in that same
study, in punishing dryness,

00:02:41.343 --> 00:02:45.643
below 5% humidity, one stress
measure actually got worse.

00:02:45.643 --> 00:02:47.043
It is not a force field.

00:02:47.411 --> 00:02:50.751
It is better understood as a
supporting ingredient that may help

00:02:51.001 --> 00:02:54.431
skin handle dehydration and
environmental stress more comfortably.

00:02:55.048 --> 00:02:58.888
So, does it do
anything to actual people?

00:02:58.948 --> 00:03:01.128
In one randomized double blind study,

00:03:01.128 --> 00:03:06.388
104 women used a cream containing
2% ectoin against the same

00:03:06.388 --> 00:03:08.428
cream without any ectoin at all.

00:03:12.429 --> 00:03:14.299
On the study's own measure,

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:16.849
the women themselves preferred
the ectoin cream.

00:03:17.089 --> 00:03:18.589
That is a real result.

00:03:18.589 --> 00:03:21.009
And it is a preference, not
a machine reading their skin.

00:03:21.447 --> 00:03:25.827
A second randomized study followed 65
people with mild to moderate

00:03:25.907 --> 00:03:27.527
atopic dermatitis, eczema.

00:03:27.527 --> 00:03:31.617
Over four weeks, an ectoin cream
performed about as well as

00:03:31.617 --> 00:03:34.967
the barrier cream it was tested
against and was well tolerated.

00:03:35.788 --> 00:03:36.788
Encouraging.

00:03:36.788 --> 00:03:38.978
Not proof that ectoincures eczema,

00:03:38.978 --> 00:03:42.728
reverses aging, or replaces
anything a dermatologist prescribes.

00:03:43.364 --> 00:03:46.154
and the evidence base
is genuinely small.

00:03:46.154 --> 00:03:50.914
Search PubMed today and you will
find 12 ectoin clinical trials. 12

00:03:51.537 --> 00:03:55.197
Some of that research also comes
from people who sell the

00:03:55.197 --> 00:03:57.657
ingredient Btop, Merck, Cow.

00:03:57.727 --> 00:04:01.137
So promising supporting ingredient, yes,

00:04:01.137 --> 00:04:02.977
miracle molecule, no.

00:04:03.452 --> 00:04:07.122
Ectoin is most interesting if
your skin runs dry,

00:04:07.262 --> 00:04:11.722
sensitive, over cleansed, or irritated
by a strong routine.

00:04:11.812 --> 00:04:14.192
It sits comfortably alongside panthenol,

00:04:14.192 --> 00:04:16.342
glycerin, squalane, and ceramide.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:20.524
But do not buy it off the
front of the bottle. Turn it around.

00:04:20.654 --> 00:04:22.544
Plenty of brands do
print a number.

00:04:22.674 --> 00:04:24.704
Paula's Choice says 7%.

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.244
The Ordinary says two.

00:04:26.526 --> 00:04:29.756
And Abebe's Ectoin Panthenol 11%?

00:04:30.006 --> 00:04:31.976
That 11 is the two
of them added together.

00:04:32.326 --> 00:04:35.116
On the ingredient list,
Panthenol is second.

00:04:35.116 --> 00:04:36.636
Ectoin is eleventh.

00:04:36.726 --> 00:04:39.636
The big number on the front
is not always the Ectoin number.

00:04:40.051 --> 00:04:44.741
The rest is judgment, not
evidence. Is it fragrance-free?

00:04:44.911 --> 00:04:45.971
If fragrance bothers you.

00:04:46.421 --> 00:04:49.051
Does the formula carry
other useful moisturizers?

00:04:49.051 --> 00:04:53.051
One good ingredient cannot rescue
a badly built product.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.860
K-beauty did not invent Ectoin.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.440
What Korean formulators are doing well
is pairing it with barrier

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.620
ingredients in light, wearable textures.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:05.925
That fits the wider move away
from aggressive transformation and towards

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.745
skin that simply stays comfortable.

00:05:07.745 --> 00:05:10.735
You will already find it
in Korean barrier serums,

00:05:10.845 --> 00:05:14.805
toners, and sun products, often in
smaller type than the trend suggests.

00:05:15.295 --> 00:05:18.465
So next time you see
ectoane on an ingredient list,

00:05:18.605 --> 00:05:20.215
remember what you are looking at.

00:05:20.215 --> 00:05:23.135
A survival strategy, borrowed from bacteria,

00:05:23.135 --> 00:05:25.095
not the new hyaluronic acid,

00:05:25.095 --> 00:05:28.855
not a miracle, a
genuinely interesting supporting molecule.

00:05:29.383 --> 00:05:32.383
Here is the one thing worth
doing turn the bottle around

00:05:32.383 --> 00:05:36.233
and find the actual percentage before
you buy and tell me

00:05:36.383 --> 00:05:39.823
Would you put a bacteria-made
survival molecule on your face?
